  "comments": "Varieties of Asoka Lion on the obverse:<br />\r\nType A: Asoka Column 15mm tall, fur rows (5) on right lion curve away from body<br />\r\nType B: Asoka Column 14mm tall, fur rows (3-4) on right lion curve away from body<br />\r\nType C: Asoka Column 13mm tall, fur rows on right lion parallel to body, fur rows on central lion neat looking, thick legs.<br />\r\nType D: Asoka Column 13mm tall, fur rows on right lion parallel to body, fur rows on central lion messy looking, thin legs.<br /><br />\r\nThe Type C die was apparently re-cut to produce Type D. As such, some collectors don&#039;t recognise types C and D as separate varieties.<br /><br />\r\nVarieties in the map exist.<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/603fd8a1003fc.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/603fd8a1003fc.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"235\" /></a><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6045bb569300d.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6045bb569300d.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"159\" /></a>",
